      "dom_id": "question-7375",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Write $y=2x-10$ in standard form.",
      "worked_solution": "Our goal is to write the equation in the form $ax+by=c,$ where $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors and $a\\ge 0.$\n\nWe begin by moving all of the variables to the left-hand side and all of the constants to the right-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n-2x+y=-10\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =-10 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2x+y) & =(-1)\\cdot (-10) \\\\ 2x-y & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors, and $a\\ge 0.$ So we are done!\n\nThe standard form of the line is $2x-y=10.$",
